                        "entry_id": "fc6eb121-53e8-3e14-89a2-d5584b60a36a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A drug that numbs the pain in the body."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e9abc258-8cc8-4857-b50c-bcdccdcf4fbb",
                                "sense_id": "f07dd0dc-a517-3f45-af74-85c31682740d",
                                "text": "Near-synonym: analgesia"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "77df49f2-bc20-4ab1-b075-049c466ec979",
                                "sense_id": "f07dd0dc-a517-3f45-af74-85c31682740d",
                                "text": "While taking one pill and dying is rare, dying accidentally after using painkillers inappropriately is common. […] The prescription painkiller Emily Jackson took is a respiratory depressant that slows breathing. That in combination with the alcohol, another respiratory depressant, overwhelmed her brain, which stopped giving her heart and lungs the signal to keep functioning."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
